              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Washington State Department of Social Services, the question presented is whether a representative payee, appointed by the commissioner of Social Security, violates the anti\u2011alienation provision of 42\u202fU.S.C.\u202f\u00a7\u202f407(a) when it uses Social Security benefits to pay for the beneficiary\u2019s current maintenance, and the Department says the answer is no."
      }
    ],
