            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens asked: \u201cCan a set\u2011off ever be legal process?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f00dbdec4b133a652495a9bec0ea67ee1c61f236b1e5bd61246dce141c972b3b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f00dbdec4b13-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens asked whether the State has any set\u2011off rights that private entities do not, asking: \u201cSuppose a private person were the representative payee. Do they have the same sort of set\u2011off rights for other debts as the State does?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f00dbdec4b133a652495a9bec0ea67ee1c61f236b1e5bd61246dce141c972b3b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f00dbdec4b13-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens further asked about \u00a7\u202f407, noting that the attorney general indicated the State could set off a tax debt under that provision."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Oral Argument",
